quity markets. A proximal policy optimization agent trained on 10 years of L3 order book data learns execution strategies that minimize market impact while achieving target fill rates. Backtesting across 2018-2023 demonstrates Sharpe ratio of 2.34, outperforming TWAP and VWAP benchmarks by 18.3 basis points per trade. Transaction cost analysis confirms profitability after realistic slippage and market impact assumptions.','General / Best Fit','2026-04-02 17:42:51.753544',1),(116,'We apply deep reinforcement learning to develop an adaptive trading strategy for high-frequency equity markets. A proximal policy optimization agent trained on 10 years of L3 order book data learns execution strategies that minimize market impact while achieving target fill rates. Backtesting across 2018-2023 demonstrates Sharpe ratio of 2.34, outperforming TWAP and VWAP benchmarks by 18.3 basis points per trade. Transaction cost analysis confirms profitability after realistic slippage and market impact assumptions.','Cross-disciplinary Science','2026-04-02 17:44:51.200855',1),(117,'This study evaluates the effectiveness of a knowledge graph-based adaptive learning system for undergraduate calculus education. A randomized controlled trial with 847 students across three universities compared adaptive instruction against traditional lecture-based learning. Students in the adaptive condition showed 23% improvement in midterm scores and 31% higher retention rates at end-of-semester assessment. Learning analytics revealed that immediate feedback and spaced repetition scheduling drove the largest performance gains.','General / Best Fit','2026-04-02 17:48:13.822661',1),(118,'This study evaluates the effectiveness of a knowledge graph-based adaptive learning system for undergraduate calculus education. A randomized controlled trial with 847 students across three universities compared adaptive instruction against traditional lecture-based learning. Students in the adaptive condition showed 23% improvement in midterm scores and 31% higher retention rates at end-of-semester assessment. Learning analytics revealed that immediate feedback and spaced repetition scheduling drove the largest performance gains.','Cross-disciplinary Science','2026-04-02 17:51:00.531626',1),(119,'We present a BERT-based automated essay scoring system trained on 50,000 argumentative essays from university entrance examinations. The model predicts holistic scores and provides dimension-level feedback on argument structure, evidence quality, and linguistic coherence. Quadratic weighted kappa of 0.89 is achieved against expert human raters. A calibration study confirms the model maintains fairness across student demographic groups with no statistically significant score bias by gender or first language background.','General / Best Fit','2026-04-02 17:53:55.276321',1),(120,'We present a BERT-based automated essay scoring system trained on 50,000 argumentative essays from university entrance examinations. The model predicts holistic scores and provides dimension-level feedback on argument structure, evidence quality, and linguistic coherence. Quadratic weighted kappa of 0.89 is achieved against expert human raters. A calibration study confirms the model maintains fairness across student demographic groups with no statistically significant score bias by gender or first language background.','Cross-disciplinary Science','2026-04-02 17:56:09.172810',1),(121,'Developing new drugs remains prohibitively expensive, time-consuming, and often involves safety issues. Accurate prediction of drug-target interactions (DTIs) can guide the drug discovery process and thus facilitate drug development. Non-Euclidian data such as drug-like molecule structures, key pocket residue structures, and protein interaction networks can be represented effectively using graphs. Therefore, the emerging graph neural network has been rapidly applied to predict DTIs, and proved effective in finding repositioning drugs and accelerating drug discovery. In this review, we provide a brief overview of deep neural networks used in DTI models. Then, we summarize the database required for DTI prediction, followed by a comprehensive introduction of applications of graph neural networks for DTI prediction. We also highlight current challenges and future directions to guide the further development of this field.','General / Best Fit','2026-04-02 17:59:12.541566',1),(122,'Developing new drugs remains prohibitively expensive, time-consuming, and often involves safety issues. Accurate prediction of drug-target interactions (DTIs) can guide the drug discovery process and thus facilitate drug development. Non-Euclidian data such as drug-like molecule structures, key pocket residue structures, and protein interaction networks can be represented effectively using graphs. Therefore, the emerging graph neural network has been rapidly applied to predict DTIs, and proved effective in finding repositioning drugs and accelerating drug discovery. In this review, we provide a brief overview of deep neural networks used in DTI models. Then, we summarize the database required for DTI prediction, followed by a comprehensive introduction of applications of graph neural networks for DTI prediction. We also highlight current challenges and future directions to guide the further development of this field.','Cross-disciplinary Science','2026-04-02 18:02:43.496395',1),(123,'Developing new drugs remains prohibitively expensive, time-consuming, and often involves safety issues. Accurate prediction of drug-target interactions (DTIs) can guide the drug discovery process and thus facilitate drug development. Non-Euclidian data such as drug-like molecule structures, key pocket residue structures, and protein interaction networks can be represented effectively using graphs. Therefore, the emerging graph neural network has been rapidly applied to predict DTIs, and proved effective in finding repositioning drugs and accelerating 